SWEET WLAN firmware identity table + review 0129-0132 F1/F5 (patch 0147, plan 2026-11-14_oriole-oneshot-2 step W0, user decision D1). Levels 1-3 unchanged.
(a) The single level-6 pin (SWW_FW_LEN 1764018 / SWW_FW_CRC 0x1153ccff, bluejay, run wd3) becomes a table of known identities swl_fwids[]: bluejay {1764018, 0x1153ccff} and oriole
    {1764091, 0x92567396} (container line of run wlan-oriole-l4; host zlib.crc32 of the stock oriole vendor fw_bcmdhd.bin, sha256 8a52ffe1). swl_fw_known(len, crc) accepts exactly one row; it replaces
    every former pin check (0132: swl_wr SWT_RV, swl_fw_pin, glue rv_ok). Glue: from level 4 on, an image that is not a table identity is not handed to stage 3 (x.img = NULL: W8 stops, zero stores),
    so the copy (W10) and the reset vector (W14) only ever see a pinned identity whose CRC swl_img_check() recomputes from the bytes.
(b) SWW_RAM_MIN 1791226 -> 1791299, so SWW_IMG_MAX = 1764091 B (441023 words, SWW_IMG_END 0x3AEAFC < SWW_WIN_TAIL 0x400000); observed RAM 2752512 B (ram_end 0x4a0000, run wlan-oriole-l3) >= RAM_MIN.
(c) F1: swl_restore() sends a config-space restore (cfg 0x84 := 0) only while swl_lpre() (the RC-local half of the 0124 preconditions: PHY isolation, link L0, ATU r0/r1) holds; else it reports
    "restore of group N skipped, link precondition P" and restore=skipped. swl_wpre() calls swl_lpre() first (same checks, same order as before).
(d) F5: every stop prints "SWEET WLAN: left after stop: atu_r2=.. sys_mem=.. ca7=.. cfg84=.. cfg80=last window selected; armed .. restored .. tuples .." (no bus access).
Tests: shim/wlan_wr_host_test.c (fwid, f1_cfg_restore), tools/test_wlan_wr_mutants.py. HW-WRITE path: review docs/reviews/0147-wlan-fw-ident-review-fable-*.md.

